"origin":395,"position":0},"title":"Making an interactive sound installation","date":"May 15, 2013","format":false,"excerpt":"What I will explain how Bendik Hovik Kjeldsberg and I made an interactive sound installation. Why We were invited to make a sound installation. How I will go trough the process and discuss some issues we encountered. \u2014\u2014\u2013 About the exhibition: Bendik Hovik Kjeldsberg and I were invited by Bilder\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/p1105.jpg?fit=960%2C540&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":1169,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2012\/10\/08\/making-a-song-from-samples-of-an-iron-monument\/","url_meta":{"origin":395,"position":1},"title":"Making a song from samples of an iron monument","date":"October 8, 2012","format":false,"excerpt":"What: I made a song based on samples from an iron monument. Why: I was hired to do it. How: I sampled the monument and processed the samples in Ableton Live. \u2014\u2014\u2013 Finished piece: Download: Ableton Live Project Preface: The museum \"Maihaugen\" in Lillehammer, Norway, hired me to do an\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/p1169.jpg?fit=1024%2C576&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":248,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/10\/10\/music-ambience-project\/","url_meta":{"origin":395,"position":2},"title":"Music &#8211; Ambience Project","date":"October 10, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"This is an excerpt from a two hour performance at the Norwegian Academy of Music early 2011. Everyone in my live electronics class were placed all over the school, playing ambient music. I was in the canteen. The whole session was improvised. I used only my computer running Ableton Live.\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/p248.jpg?fit=640%2C360&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":35,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/controllers-launchpad\/","url_meta":{"origin":395,"position":3},"title":"Controllers (launchpad)","date":"September 13, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"I started with what I already had, a Launchpad from Novation. In the aspect of diversity and portability, this controller presents many advantages. You have 64 + 16 buttons (8x8)+(2x8) located at a fairly small space, and you can flip through pages which multiplies your number of buttons endlessly. You\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"launchpad","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/6.jpg?fit=550%2C550&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":25,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/09\/13\/signal-flow\/","url_meta":{"origin":395,"position":4},"title":"Signal-flow","date":"September 13, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"The audio from my EMFit based contact microphones goes into my sound card (Focusrite pro40), then to the DAW - Ableton Live, through desired effects and\/or to be stored on the hard drive, back to the sound card and out to a PA-system. Sound engineers usually treat my drums as\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"signal-flow","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2011\/09\/41.gif?fit=586%2C476&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]},{"id":324,"url":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/2011\/10\/11\/music-skrr\/","url_meta":{"origin":395,"position":5},"title":"Music &#8211; SkRR","date":"October 11, 2011","format":false,"excerpt":"SkRR is a sound collective based in Oslo. We arrange concerts, workshops and social gatherings where we focus on production and performance of electronic music, sound design, sound programming and experimenting with auditive and visual expressions. You can follow SkRR on: Twitter (Norwegian) Origo (Norwegian) . Here is a concert\u2026","rel":"","context":"In &quot;ALL&quot;","img":{"alt_text":"","src":"https:\/\/i0.wp.com\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/8\/2013\/05\/p324.jpg?fit=1200%2C675&ssl=1&resize=350%2C200","width":350,"height":200},"classes":[]}],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/395"}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=395"}],"version-history":[{"count":1,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/395\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":1901,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/395\/revisions\/1901"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1755"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=395"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=395"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/drumsandelectronics.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=395"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}